winpe-terminal (0.1.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * postrm purge removes WPT's four directories with rm -rf again. Preserving
    unknown files left the state and log directories behind after a purge,
    which made the uninstall look incomplete; those directories are created by
    postinst and hold only WPT-managed content.

 -- winpe_terminal contributors <noreply@example.invalid>  Sun, 01 Nov 2026 03:20:00 +0800

winpe-terminal (0.1.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * prepare shows what it is doing: every step is flushed immediately and
    curl draws a progress bar, so a long download no longer looks like a hang.
  * Add --accept-microsoft-license for an explicit non-interactive consent
    (the licence text is still printed; nothing is accepted silently).

 -- winpe_terminal contributors <noreply@example.invalid>  Sun, 01 Nov 2026 03:05:00 +0800

winpe-terminal (0.1.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * postrm purge: rmdir --ignore-fail-on-non-empty always succeeded, so files
    that WPT does not own were never reported. Purge now removes WPT's own
    instance logs and reports anything else it leaves behind, keeping the
    directory instead of silently claiming a clean sweep.

